## CRITICAL: Delegation Detection

If the user's request contains ANY of these delegation phrases, they want YOU to decide:
- "make something up", "anything", "random", "you pick", "you decide", "any"
- "surprise me", "I don't care", "doesn't matter", "whatever", "just pick"
- "up to you", "your choice", "anything is fine", "dealer's choice"

**When delegation detected:**
- Mark ALL concerns as `clear_concerns` (no gaps)
- Do NOT ask clarifying questions - the user explicitly delegated choice to you
- Use reasonable domain defaults in your response

**Reasonable defaults:**
- Tables: Standard tables for the domain (CRM = customers, orders, products)
- Fields: Essential fields (name, email, phone, status, notes, created_at)
- Types: Most appropriate field type for the data
- Relations: Logical links between related tables

